Subject: [PATCH] AMLAudioTrim: only on the AML card's own devices

The trim holds the audio clock to the picture by moving mpll0, and while
it holds, the player leaves its own clock alone (11_30). It engaged for
any device Kodi played to, so with Virtual Sound chosen - a loopback the
binaural daemon reads at its own pace, and plays out of the AML card
itself - it measured the loopback's rate as a drift of nearly 1000 ppm,
refused that as no rate a clock runs at, and kept dithering mpll0 under
the daemon's output, while the player, told the trim was holding,
corrected nothing: the picture slipped against the sound, frames were
dropped and repeated, and the daemon's output, trimmed underneath it,
ran dry now and then and clicked.

It now engages only when the device the stream plays on is the AML
card's (its ALSA name carries CARD=AML). Any other card, a loopback, a
USB DAC, keeps its own time, and the player corrects against it as it
does everywhere else.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLAudioTrim.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLAudioTrim.h   |  4 ++++
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp     |  8 +++++++-
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLAudioTrim.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLAudioTrim.cpp
@@ -271,6 +271,18 @@
   return Node().reachesPcm;
 }
 
+bool CAMLAudioTrim::ReachesSink(bool passthrough)
+{
+  const auto component = CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent();
+  const auto settings = component ? component->GetSettings() : nullptr;
+  if (!settings)
+    return false;
+  const std::string device =
+      settings->GetString(passthrough ? CSettings::SETTING_AUDIOOUTPUT_PASSTHROUGHDEVICE
+                                      : CSettings::SETTING_AUDIOOUTPUT_AUDIODEVICE);
+  return device.find("CARD=AML") != std::string::npos;
+}
+
 bool CAMLAudioTrim::WriteLevel(int level)
 {
   try
